./LOGBOOK.md:1379:- FINDING: The first runtime gate sent SIGTERM and immediately closed stdin. On a fresh pinned Go 1.26.5 build, EOF occasionally won the race and the relay exited 0 before its signal owner produced the required exit 130; an older retained artifact happened to pass, so a single green smoke did not expose the harness defect.
./LOGBOOK.md:1423:### 0825 — M0-bound macOS and deterministic harness runtime factories (TASK-260715-3ejhyy)
./LOGBOOK.md:1424:- IMPLEMENTATION: The macOS production call site validates the exact accepted manifest SHA-256 and semantic evidence before any component closure runs, derives the accepted packet/HEV/SSH values from that manifest, and creates one fresh coordinator graph per generation. The graph selects `LibSSH2TransportFactory`, the system-domain Keychain resolver, mandatory approved-host-policy and privacy-safe mapper inputs, injected TCP/DNS and network-settings seams, and a bridge-backed M1 packet plane. The deterministic SPM harness implements the same candidate-neutral `TunnelRuntimeFactory` without a production-manifest bypass.
./LOGBOOK.md:1427:- VERIFICATION: The focused composition and harness suites pass 10/10; the final full SwiftPM run passes 504 tests in 42 suites with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues. Strict Swift format, Core boundary guard, 32 M0 binding negatives, accepted manifest/repository validation, native/libssh2 pin inspection, three SPM target builds, and unsigned macOS Debug/Release host/provider generation, target tests, linkage, and graph validation all exit 0. The first focused compile and first lint run exited 1 on test-double types and mechanical formatting, then passed after correction. The first provider gate exited 2 before generation because the task worktree's two-line Tuist pin was untrusted; after explicitly trusting that exact `mise.toml`, pinned Tuist 4.202.5 validation passed.
./LOGBOOK.md:1430:- EXACT-GRAPH EVIDENCE: The macOS smoke now drives the runtime returned by `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory` through immutable profile load, host-policy evaluation, credential lookup, authentication, TCP/DNS prepare, packet preflight, settings application, and packet activation. It proves zero descriptor/listener/HEV/read acquisition through preflight, one acquisition per generation after settings, and reverse idempotent teardown after repeated stop. The deterministic harness drives its own returned runtime through the same lifecycle and cleanup contract.
./LOGBOOK.md:1432:- REWORK VERIFICATION: Focused composition, exact macOS ownership, and exact harness ownership suites pass 13/13. The full SwiftPM suite passes 507 tests in 43 suites with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues. Core, macOS adapter, and harness-support target builds; strict recursive Swift format; Core/security-boundary checks; accepted M0 validation; all 32 M0 negative tests; native/libssh2 pin checks; `git diff --check`; and unsigned generated macOS host/provider Debug+Release validation all exit 0. Three intermediate compile attempts and the first task-scoped lint correctly exited 1 during the API/test-double rework and remain in `.temp/TASK-260715-3ejhyy/`.
./LOGBOOK.md:1434:- REVIEW REWORK 2: Revision 2 exposed Foundation boolean type confusion: `NSNumber(1) as? Bool` let numeric JSON `1` satisfy `productionCompositionPermitted`. The semantic validator now requires the value's Core Foundation type to be `CFBoolean`; numeric `0` and `1` both fail with `compositionNotPermitted`. Restoring the permissive cast made the named negative test exit 1, and restoring the guard made it pass. Focused composition and exact macOS/harness ownership tests, the 508-test/43-suite SwiftPM run (25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues), both production build targets, strict format, Core/native/M0 gates, 32 manifest negatives, and the unsigned macOS provider matrix all exit 0.
./LOGBOOK.md:1435:### 1010 — Composed M1 runtime harness owns deterministic lifecycle evidence (TASK-260715-m8bi8i)
./LOGBOOK.md:1439:- MUTATION ANOMALY/FIX: The first `8 -> 7` cap narrowing remained green because the test derived both accepted and rejected values from the production constant, making its evidence self-minted. The test now owns independent contract literals 8 and 9. With production still narrowed to 7 the complete M1 harness suite exited 1; after restoring 8 it passed. Two earlier probes that returned 0 are retained and explicitly do not count as negative evidence.
./LOGBOOK.md:1440:- RESOURCE/PRIVACY EVIDENCE: Each generation uses real process-owned socket-pair descriptors and a controlled native borrow, joins the packet read and bridge tasks, closes the TCP channel, and requires zero descriptor, task, channel, socket, and native-runtime residue. The fixture manifest and validator reject dependency drift, raw profile output, nonzero growth gauges, unexpected stdout/stderr, and exit drift without retaining packet, DNS, endpoint, credential, or profile data.
